@gribnoysup You could use [`schema-utils`](https://github.com/webpack-contrib/schema-utils) for that purpose as standardize way for plugins/loaders. If you need anything feel free to open an issue in `webpack-contrib/schema-utils`

```js
const schema = require("../schemas/plugins/bannerPluginSchema.json");
const validateOptions = require("schema-utils");

class Plugin {
  constructor (options) {
     validateOptions(schema, options, `${name}` /* <= Banner Plugin */)
  }
}
```

